  "problem": "${\\int }_{0}^{6}\u27e8{e}^{-t},\\,4{t}^{2}\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t=$",
  "worked_solution": "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}\u27e8{e}^{-t},\\,4{t}^{2}\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & =\u27e8{\\int }_{0}^{6}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,{\\int }_{0}^{6}4{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8(-{e}^{-t}){|}_{0}^{6},\\,\\frac{4}{3}{t}^{3}\\,{|}_{0}^{6}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-{e}^{-6}+{e}^{-0},\\,\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot {6}^{3}-\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e81-\\frac{1}{{e}^{6}},\\,288\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
